        <obo:IAO_0000115>Anatomical structure, which has as its parts a heterogeneous collection of  organs, organ parts, cells, cell parts or body part subdivisions that are adjacent to, or continuous with one another; does not constitute a cell part, cell,  tissue,  organ, organ system or organ system subdivision, cardinal body part, body part subdivision or anatomical junction. Examples: joint, adnexa of uterus, root of lung, renal pedicle, back.</obo:IAO_0000115>
